# Generated by .claude/scripts/setup_docs_worktree.sh — personal, machine-specific paths.
*.code-workspace
# Running examples/config_builder.py leaves examples/__pycache__/ behind, which
# showed up as untracked for whoever ran it. Byte-code, never shared.
__pycache__/
# The legacy C++ is TRACKED, in legacy/. It used to be ignored at the repo root, which meant the
# implementation the Rust is ported from lived on one laptop — and a doc comment citing it pointed
# at a file nobody else had. It is reference, not a build target; see legacy/README.md.
handoff_transfer_from_c++.md
handoff_edge_multiplicity_cap_simplification.md
**/target/

# .claude machinery is tracked; only personal settings are not.
#
# CHANGED 2026-08-13: `.claude/work/current/` used to be ignored, on the grounds that two people must
# not fight over one live plan. That reason is now served by the PATH rather than by ignoring —
# live tasks live in `work/<owner>/current/` and `work/<owner>/parked/<slug>/`, so neither owner
# ever writes to the other's directory and there is nothing to fight over.
#
# They are TRACKED because the point is to pick a task up on ANOTHER MACHINE. An ignored plan lives
# on one laptop, which is the same failure that made `work/archive/` tracked earlier: a /done was
# stranded wherever it was run. `/save` commits and pushes `work/<owner>/` as its last step, so the
# handoff a second machine reads is the one the first machine wrote.
#
# The remaining hazard is you-versus-you, not you-versus-James: two machines editing the same
# `work/<owner>/current/plan.md`. That is why handoff.md carries a `Machine:` stamp and /load stops
# and reports on divergence instead of merging a plan file. See .claude/CLAUDE.md.
.claude/settings.local.json

# .claude/ is its own repository now - md12ol/GET-claude, cloned as this directory.
# Agreed at the joint meeting of 2026-08-13 (GitHub #74). Keeping it out of GET is what
# keeps it out of every clone, every release branch and the built wheel.
.claude/
